WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.267
-We love you.
Michael Strahan.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:03.434
-Hey. I got you.
I love you guys.

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:04.767
Thank you so much for that.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.067
-And always got to shout-out
my guys, The Roots.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.167
Thank you guys, man, for playing
that "Fly Like the Eagles."

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:11.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.567
-You like that, right?
-They think they're slick.

00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:15.501
-Yeah.
-Football season's not here yet.

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.834
You're always strutting
with the Eagles stuff.

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:20.300
It's all good. I'll be back
when we're stomping you guys.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.901
But it's okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:23.667
-You know, this is the --
Do you know that this is

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:25.801
the 17th time you've --
you appeared on our show.

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:27.701
-I can't believe it.
-And it's a record for us.

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.734
Most appearance
by any guest ever is you,

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:30.868
Michael Strahan, on our show.
-Really?

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:31.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.801
Really?
Wow!

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.100
-And I'm so happy
that you've come back.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.200
And thank you.
-Thank you, man.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.534
-You're a great guest.

00:00:37.534 --> 00:00:39.567
-Well, I love being here, man.
I love being here.

00:00:39.567 --> 00:00:40.901
It's like family.
You guys are great.

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.467
You have the best audience
in television.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:45.334
So, thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.334 --> 00:00:46.734
-Even though The Roots
give you a hard time.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:47.801
You know we love you.
-Yeah, I love it, though.

00:00:47.801 --> 00:00:48.868
-Roots give you a hard time.

00:00:48.868 --> 00:00:50.634
They got it.
They're Philly.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.367
I always have so many things
to talk to you about.

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:55.400
And this one, I cannot wait
to talk to you about.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.334
'Cause this -- we haven't
talked about this.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.968
And we're friends,
but we've not talked about this.

00:00:58.968 --> 00:01:01.367
-Mm-hmm.
-You went to space.

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.200
-I did.
I went to space!

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.267
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
-You did the Jeff Bezos --

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.767
you did the Blue Origin rocket.
-Yeah, man.

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.567
-Look at this.
That's you.

00:01:09.567 --> 00:01:10.634
-That's me.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.601
-Now was that before
you took off?

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:17.334
Or is this when you landed?
-That was, um --

00:01:17.334 --> 00:01:19.367
That's actually
when we're going up.

00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:20.534
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:20.534 --> 00:01:22.667
And it's, like,
it's pushing my face back.

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:23.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:26.133
So, you start with a smile,
and it gets bigger.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.334
Only thing it didn't do was
push my teeth together, but...

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:29.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:29.334 --> 00:01:31.467
It was --
It was incredible.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:32.667
It was absolutely --
-Now, talk to me.

00:01:32.667 --> 00:01:35.067
Please tell me.
What -- What -- What --

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:36.834
-It was the most incredible
thing I've ever done.

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.100
-You're wearing the outfit.
You're strapped in,

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.367
you go, "Here you go,"
you take off,

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:44.000
and then you're like --
Do you wait for a ding?

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.667
Like a, "boong!" -- "You can
take your seat belt off now"?

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:51.267
-No. You're sitting there,
and you hear the countdown.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.033
And they're counting down,
and you're thinking,

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.400
"Okay, it's too late.
Can't get off.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.234
I'm in it.
Let's just do it."

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.267
-Oh, my God.
-And then, it takes off,

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:01.234
and it starts rumbling,
and the cabin turns red

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.067
from all the flames from below.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:05.400
-And then it was like --
It feels like you're in a movie.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.033
Like, I feel like I'm, like,
in "Apollo 13" movie.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:09.901
Like, thing is shaking,
and it says,

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.734
"You've cleared the tower,"
and literally every one of us,

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:17.234
all six of us, just let out
the biggest happy yell.

00:02:17.234 --> 00:02:19.701
Because it was like
all this pressure and relief.

00:02:19.701 --> 00:02:21.801
And then, once you get
to a certain point,

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:25.200
you realize you're going over
2,000 miles per hour,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:26.868
and you're hitting
all these G's,

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:29.000
and next thing you know,
you're at 40,000 feet.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.801
You're like, "Oh, I've been
in a plane that high."

00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:33.634
Then you look, and you're
200,000 or 300,000 feet.

00:02:33.634 --> 00:02:37.534
And then they release
the capsule from the rocket,

00:02:37.534 --> 00:02:40.901
and you're body goes...

00:02:40.901 --> 00:02:42.901
And then the light goes off.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.834
And it goes "Ding!
You are free to roam the cabin."

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.667
-No!
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:49.334
I was waiting for it!
Like, yeah!

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.567
Tie me up and go --

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.901
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:55.834
You got me!
You got me.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.434
-The light does goes off,
and then you undo your belt.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:02:59.767
It was surreal.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:02.000
And you should come with me
next time, man.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
Me and you!

00:03:04.334 --> 00:03:07.133
Let's go!

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:09.801
-I'm busy that --
I'm busy that weekend.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:11.868
-I'll give you a date.
I'm busy that week--

00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:13.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:14.968
Would you ever go --
would you go back?

00:03:14.968 --> 00:03:17.267
-You know what?
When I got off the rocket,

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:20.701
Jeff Bezos said, "Next time,
we'll go to the Moon."

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.300
-Oh, my God.
-And I was so fired up,

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:24.367
I'm like, "Yeah!"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.667
And now I think about it,
I'm like, "I don't know!"

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.667
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.968
You're always a very,
very busy man.

00:03:30.968 --> 00:03:34.400
You have your own menswear line,
very successful.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.100
You have your own skin care line
coming out this fall.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.000
-Yeah, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.334
-What is that called?
-It's called skin care.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:43.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.734 --> 00:03:44.934
-Is that the name of it?
-Yeah.

00:03:44.934 --> 00:03:46.601
It's called skin care,
Michael Strahan.

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:47.767
-It's called skin care?
-Yeah.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:48.801
Michael Strahan.
-There you go.

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.367
You just laid it out.
-Same thing.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:51.834
-Wow.
-But it's coming out

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:53.200
in the fall.
-All right.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:56.033
So in the fall we'll talk.
Will you come back for that?

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.200
-You know,
I can't throw it out there now.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:59.234
They told me,
"Don't say too much about it now

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.234
'cause it's not out yet."
So I can't say anything.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:02.567
-Let's not
say anything about it.

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.167
-Yes. I got to come back in
for the 18th time.

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:05.400
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.734
18's the lucky number.
-18's the lucky number.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:10.334
-And then you
have this production company

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:12.100
with Tom Brady.
-Yeah.

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.934
-Religion of Sports.
-Yes.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:15.400
-It just won another
sports Emmy, by the way.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.834
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:04:16.834 --> 00:04:18.534
-You keep winning these awards.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.534 --> 00:04:20.033
Well done.

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.801
Did you guys talk about
when he was about to retire?

00:04:22.801 --> 00:04:25.334
-Oh, absolutely.
Yeah, I played golf with him.

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.767
And we're playing golf,
and I'm telling him, I'm like,

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:29.968
"Dude, let me tell you,
when you're done,

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.067
you will never
strap a helmet on,

00:04:32.067 --> 00:04:34.200
you will never put on another
pair of shoulder pads.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.400
It's done.

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:37.734
Like, you just won't do it
ever again."

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:39.601
And I knew
he wasn't gonna retire.

00:04:39.601 --> 00:04:41.601
I knew he wasn't.
He wasn't done.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:44.701
You know, Tom,
he's turning 45 tomorrow.

00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.667
Happy birthday, Tom Brady.
-Yeah, happy birthday Tom Brady.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:50.567
-Turning 45 tomorrow.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:50.567 --> 00:04:53.334
And I don't know
how he keeps on going.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:55.234
But I can tell
he still wants to get

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:57.667
every bit of football
out of him.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:59.334
And at that point,
after that conversation,

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.100
I realized
he wasn't gonna retire.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:03.300
-Yeah.
-So I wasted a whole tweet,

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.868
Instagram post.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.968
"Oh, congratulations, Tom Brady!
Great career!"

00:05:06.968 --> 00:05:08.334
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.634
You sent a really nice tweet.
Will you send it again?

00:05:10.634 --> 00:05:12.501
-I'm just gonna
retweet the same thing.

00:05:12.501 --> 00:05:13.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.901 --> 00:05:15.067
Why?
I'm not wasting my time.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:17.067
He got it out of me once.
That's good enough.

00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:19.133
-Just gonna cut and paste?
-Yeah, cut and paste, man.

00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:20.601
-Just cut and paste.
Why not?

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.501
Let's talk about
"$100,000 Pyramid."

00:05:22.501 --> 00:05:26.000
-Oh, man.
-Oh, man, this is a fun show.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.767
I got a taste of, you know,
hosting a game show.

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:30.067
And it's fun.
-It is.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.934
-And you get to have all these
cool celebrities on.

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:33.868
-Yeah.
-I know Jason Alexander's

00:05:33.868 --> 00:05:35.968
come on, Wiz Khalifa was on.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.334
Do you find certain professions

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:39.567
are better
than other professions?

00:05:39.567 --> 00:05:42.100
-Yes. Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:45.133
Certain people are just better,
but definitely the professions

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.033
kind of --
comedians are really good.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:50.734
-Yeah.
-Musicians and comedians

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:53.367
are good, because their careers
are like wordplay.

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.167
You got to think about it.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:58.501
A musician is like playing with
words to make you feel emotion,

00:05:58.501 --> 00:06:00.400
and so you have to know
pretty much the dictionary.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:02.167
You know that.
-Yeah.

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:05.300
-And Wiz Khalifa was insane!
The comedians,

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.901
they're taking words
to make you laugh

00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:08.634
and make you feel
some kind of emotion.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.400
And I was surprised
because I'm like,

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.033
"Oh, a comedian -- anybody
can make anybody laugh."

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:13.367
That's just not true.

00:06:13.367 --> 00:06:15.167
"Musicians, you're just talented
at making music."

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:17.667
It's just not true.
They are so good at word play.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:19.133
-Yeah.
-And then a lot of people

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:22.000
you think are really smart,
which they are, they're just --

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.334
they're dumb at this game.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:26.434
-I want to show everyone a clip.
Here's a peek at this season

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:29.400
of "The $100,000 Pyramid."
Take a look at this.

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.634
-Oh, gosh, like,
"I'm just so drunk."

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:32.834
-Lush.
-Yep.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:34.067
And then,
another word for your butt.

00:06:34.067 --> 00:06:35.000
Your --
-Tush.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.100
-Yep.
[ Dinging ]

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:41.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was awesome.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.834
-In the intro, I said,
"You're good with words."

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:45.334
She didn't even say anything,
you said, "Lush."

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.267
I mean, I'm like,
"Hottie -- very lush."

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.200
Okay.
-Also, she's very drunk, so...

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:54.467
-I'm wasted.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:56.834
-You got to have a good face.
You got to have a go--

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:59.567
-You got to have...

00:06:59.567 --> 00:07:02.767
But the faces are natural,
because like I said,

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:05.100
I don't know the words,
so I'm guessing along

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.334
with everybody else, man.
But it's so much fun.

00:07:07.334 --> 00:07:08.868
And hopefully
everybody enjoys it.

00:07:08.868 --> 00:07:10.234
-We love you.
Michael Strahan, everybody.

00:07:10.234 --> 00:07:13.634
"The $100,000 Pyramid"
airs Sunday nights at 9:00 p.m.

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:15.868
on ABC!
Michael and I are doing

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:17.868
something fun after the break,
so stick around.

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:18.868
Come on back.

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:20.133
Don't change that channel.
Come on.

